1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Imperial Noble Consort Jingmin (敬敏皇贵妃; Pinyin: Jìngmǐn huáng guìfēi; 17th century – 20 August 1699) was a concubine of the Kangxi Emperor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Life
2 CONT Family background
2 CONT Imperial Noble Consort Jingmin's personal name was not recorded in history. Her family belong to the Bordered White Banner.
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Haikuan (海寬) served as military commander
2 CONT Kangxi Era
2 CONT It is unclear when Imperial Noble Consort Jingmin was born or when she entered the palace. But on the first day of October in the twenty-fifth year of Kangxi (1686), she gave birth to the thirteenth prince Yinxiang. On November 27
2 CONC  in the twenty-sixth year of Kangxi, she gave birth to Princess Wenke of the Second Rank (和碩溫恪公主). And on the thirtieth year of Kangxi, she gave birth to her last child, Princess Dunke of the Second Rank (和碩敦恪公主).
2 CONT
2 CONT In the thirty-eighth year of Kangxi, Concubine Min died in Wulong Pavilion in Beihai. In July of that year, the Kangxi Emperor instructed the Minister of Ritual to promote Concubine Min to Consort Min (敏妃) posthumously. In Septemb
2 CONC er of the same year, Kangxi's third son Yunzhi was demoted to beile for not attending the funeral for Consort Min.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records show that Consort Min during the thirty-eighth year of Kangxi and was temporarily buried in the gazed flower gate in the Emperor's mausoleum. The reason for this arrangement is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the twenty-sixth of the first month of the first year of Yongzheng, Emperor Yongzheng instructed the ministry of rites to posthumously appoint Consort Min as Dowager Imperial Noble Consort (皇考皇贵妃). On June 20, her posthumous ti
2 CONC tle was changed to Imperial Noble Consort Jingmin (敬敏皇贵妃). On the first day of September, Imperial Noble Consort Jingmin along with the Kangxi Emperor and Empress Xiaogongren were buried in the Jingling Mausoleum in Zunhua City, H
2 CONC ebei Province.
2 CONT
2 CONT Titles
2 CONT During the reign of the Shunzhi Emperor (r. 1643–1661) or the Kangxi Emperor (r. 1661–1722):
2 CONT Lady Janggiya
2 CONT During the reign of the Kangxi Emperor (r. 1661–1722):
2 CONT Concubine Min (敏嬪; from 1689), fifth rank consort
2 CONT Consort Min (敏妃; fom 1699)
2 CONT During the reign of the Yongzheng Emperor (r. 1722–1735):
2 CONT Imperial Noble Consort Huangkao (皇考皇贵妃; from 26 January 1723)
2 CONT Imperial Noble Consort Jingmin (敬敏皇贵妃; from 30 June 1723)
2 CONT Issues
2 CONT As Mistress:
2 CONT Yinxiang, Prince Yixian of the First Rank (怡賢親王 胤祥; 16 November 1686 – 18 June 1730), Kangxi Emperor's 22nd (13th) son
2 CONT Princess Wenke of the Second Rank (和碩溫恪公主; 31 December 1687 – 27 July 1709), Kamgxi Emperor's 13th daughter
2 CONT As Concubine Min:
2 CONT Princess Dunke of the Second Rank (和碩敦恪公主; 3 February 1691 – 2 January 1710), Kangxi Emperor's 15th daughter
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperial_Noble_Consort_Jingmin
